trol.spec.ts` -> \"No test files found, exiting with code 1 / filter: tests/e2e/cascade-control.spec.ts / include: tests/**/*.test.ts, tests/**/*.test.tsx / exclude: tests/e2e/**/*.spec.ts\" \u2014 vitest.config.ts:28-30 explicitly excludes them, so `npm test` never touches them either.\n\nConsequence: the repo carries E2E specs that read as coverage in `ls tests/e2e/` and in any file-count metric, while nothing executes them; and this is what lets README.md:459 claim \"Integration tests: None exist\" without anyone noticing the contradiction (the sibling README row covers the claim itself).\n\nFIX (pick one and record it in the commit message):\n  (a) wire them: add @playwright/test to devDependencies, a playwright.config.ts, an npm script (e.g. \"e2e\": \"playwright test tests/e2e\"), and either a CI job or an explicit README note that the browser E2E leg is not part of CI; or\n  (b) delete the four files and record in the README test section that browser E2E is not implemented, so the tree stops advertising tests nobody runs.\nDo not leave them present-but-unrunnable.\n\nACCEPTANCE: exactly one of these holds \u2014 (a) `npx playwright test tests/e2e` exits 0 and `grep -c '@playwright/test' package.json` prints >= 1, or (b) `ls tests/e2e/*.spec.ts` exits non-zero (shell reports \"No such file or directory\") and the README's test section states that browser E2E is not implemented.\n\nch:trace row=README-14 spec=README.md#what-works-vs-what-doesnt wave=speclang-readme-2026-10-27-15-09-36#sweep test=tests/e2e/cascade-control.spec.ts::Cascade-Control-E2E doc=README.md prompt=/home/kara/.hermes/skills/coding-hermes/coding-hermes-readme/SKILL.md evidence=/home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/readme/speclang/e2e-probe.log witness=none:repository-internal-runner-gap verdict=none:open-finding commit=none:open memory=none:not-written", "ts": null, "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-10-27T15:37:45.995932+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-27T15:37:45.995932+00:00", "worker_status": "p